WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:04.145
- [Instructor] At the
edge of the solar system

00:00:04.145 --> 00:00:07.170
Pluto pushes the boundaries
of our understanding

00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:09.080
of the universe.

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:11.620
Nestled within the far flung Kuiper belt

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:14.390
the dwarf planet is believed
to be one of the countless

00:00:14.390 --> 00:00:16.741
celestial objects left
over from the formation

00:00:16.741 --> 00:00:19.420
of the solar system.

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:22.520
While it is one of the
Kuiper belts largest bodies,

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:26.500
Pluto is only half as wide as
the contiguous United States

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:29.480
and about two thirds the
size of Earth's moon.

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:32.260
Making it easily dwarfed
by the solar system's

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:34.760
eight true planets.

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:38.658
This tiny world takes 248
earth years to orbit the Sun

00:00:38.658 --> 00:00:42.000
and it does so from an average distance

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.920
of over 3.6 billion miles

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:49.020
or 40 times the space
between Earth and the Sun.

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:52.090
Such a distance from the solar
system's main source of heat

00:00:52.090 --> 00:00:55.800
causes extreme temperatures
on the dwarf planet's surface

00:00:55.800 --> 00:01:00.800
between negative 375 and
negative 400 degrees Fahrenheit.

00:01:02.764 --> 00:01:06.400
The frigid temperatures
play a crucial role

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:09.330
in shaping the geological
composition of Pluto.

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:12.100
It's core, likely made of rock and metals,

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:15.440
is encapsulated by a mantle made of ice.

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:18.360
The dwarf planet's crust
is made of rock material

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:20.410
and other types of ice such as

00:01:20.410 --> 00:01:23.820
frozen carbon monoxide,
methane and nitrogen.

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:26.210
These frozen gases cover Pluto's

00:01:26.210 --> 00:01:30.850
approximately 6.4 million
square miles of surface area.

00:01:30.850 --> 00:01:32.953
Which is barely the size of Russia.

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:35.860
The icy terrain is much like Earth's.

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:40.210
With polar ice caps,
valleys, planes and craters.

00:01:40.210 --> 00:01:43.570
It even has glaciers
made of frozen nitrogen

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:45.470
and frozen water on the surface

00:01:45.470 --> 00:01:47.793
makes giant floating mountains.

00:01:50.191 --> 00:01:51.831
(peaceful music)

00:01:51.831 --> 00:01:54.352
Such varied terrain is
influenced by the presence

00:01:54.352 --> 00:01:56.670
of weather patterns or an atmosphere.

00:01:56.670 --> 00:01:59.583
Pluto's atmosphere is thin
and reaches a high altitude

00:01:59.583 --> 00:02:02.590
due to the dwarf planet's low gravity.

00:02:02.590 --> 00:02:05.957
Which is only about 6
percent as strong as Earth's.

00:02:05.957 --> 00:02:09.980
The atmosphere's comprised
of nitrogen and methane gases

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:13.320
plus red hydrocarbon particles
that scatter sunlight

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:15.830
to give Pluto blue skies.

00:02:15.830 --> 00:02:19.603
Parts of the atmosphere may
even freeze and fall like snow.

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:24.840
Floating high above the
dwarf planet's atmosphere

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:26.450
are five moons.

00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:30.650
The largest, Charon is about
half the size of Pluto.

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:32.140
The four other moons;

00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:35.953
Nix, Hydra, Kerberos and
Styx, are much smaller.

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:39.010
While the eight true
planets were discovered

00:02:40.232 --> 00:02:41.065
by the mid-1800s.

00:02:41.065 --> 00:02:43.735
Pluto was not spotted until 1930.

00:02:43.735 --> 00:02:47.660
Pluto, named after the
Roman god of the underworld,

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:49.783
was considered the ninth planet.

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:57.315
But in 2006, Pluto lost this status.

00:02:57.315 --> 00:03:02.120
At the time, worlds similar to
Pluto were being discovered,

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:04.100
deeper in the Kuiper belt.

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:06.260
This initiated close scrutiny of Pluto

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:08.970
and the definition of a planet.

00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:12.640
The International Astronomical
Union evaluated Pluto

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:16.600
based on the characteristics
necessary to be a true planet.

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:18.210
It must orbit the Sun.

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:21.910
Is not a moon and has enough
mass and gravitational pull

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:23.980
to assume a round shape.

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:26.470
However it was the fourth characteristic

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:28.630
that compromised Pluto's status.

00:03:28.630 --> 00:03:32.110
It's inability to clear
it's orbit of debris.

00:03:32.110 --> 00:03:36.350
So Pluto was reclassified
and arguably demoted

00:03:36.350 --> 00:03:39.203
from being a true planet
to being a dwarf planet.

00:03:41.810 --> 00:03:44.132
Pluto's story represents
our evolving understanding

00:03:44.132 --> 00:03:46.200
of the universe.

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:47.890
There is always more to discover

00:03:47.890 --> 00:03:50.463
and we are continuously
reaching toward it.

